{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01DuTLQbunkBSWymX6DdrtbB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a **single-user personal productivity system** for J.C. Liechty that has grown a second major capability â€” an **R&D \"cockpit\"** for managing AI agent work. Grounded in the project docs:\n\n**Core purpose â€” a markdown-backed task/project manager**\n- It tracks tasks, projects, an inbox, and per-domain work (academic, commercial, family, writing) with **plain markdown files as the single source of truth** â€” no database, no binary formats (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`).\n- Tasks move through a defined lifecycle: Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled / Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored, each writing back to markdown.\n\n**What it ships / runs**\n- `anchor_gui.py` â€” a **stdlib-only Python HTTP server** (port 8777, run as the persistent NSSM Windows service `anchor`) that generates the full dashboard HTML and writes markdown directly via `/api/*` endpoints.\n- `anchor.py` â€” a CLI engine mirroring the same logic and generating a static `dashboard.html`.\n- `anchor_healthcheck.py` â€” a daily 5 AM self-test that parses every file, boots a throwaway server, exercises every endpoint, walks a synthetic task through all states, and writes `health_reports/`.\n\n**The R&D control surface (the bulk of recent work)**\n- Turns each project into a **\"Project Cockpit\"** that manages \"trio\" AI work â€” Research (researchPrime) â†’ Planning (Crucible) â†’ Build (Foreman) â€” as durable, isolated server-side sessions.\n- Ships **real ConPTY terminals** (xterm.js + the one declared native exception `pywinpty`), **per-session git-worktree isolation**, a **session registry**, **cached/validated AI summaries**, an **engine toggle** (Claudeâ†”Gemini), **per-lane doc roles**, a **cost/tokens/time rollup**, a **grass-ideas board**, and **type-aware deliverable launch** (skill/service/program/doc).\n- Built across versions v2 â†’ v3 (\"Mission Control\") â†’ v4 (\"Project Cockpit\"), all merged to master.\n\n**Key constraints it holds to**\n- Python **stdlib-only** (sole exception: optional `pywinpty` for terminals, which degrades gracefully if absent).\n- **Single folder** (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`), no OneDrive/syncing, local Git only; all files remain plain-text and accessible from any CLI tool.\n\nOne caveat on grounding: these claims come from `CLAUDE.md` and the locked North-Star excerpts, not from re-reading the source â€” I can verify any specific claim against the actual code if you want."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45330,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d3e90dae-b910-4301-b7e9-dc8900932245","uuid":"0ee8075c-688b-452e-96eb-e1539da974bb","request_id":"req_011Cc1vsLyouNvEfNp9J7vsi"}
